.com/photo/msid-133018797,imgsize-73454.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Mignon McLaughlin: 'The proud man can learn humility, but he will be proud of it' and why some things never change]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133015587.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-mignon-mclaughlin-the-proud-man-can-learn-humility-but-he-will-be-proud-of-it-and-why-some-things-never-change/articleshow/133015587.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-mignon-mclaughlin-the-proud-man-can-learn-humility-but-he-will-be-proud-of-it-and-why-some-things-never-change/articleshow/133015587.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T02:15:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133015617,imgsize-34602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote by Michel Foucault: 'Maybe the target nowadays is not to discover what we are but...']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133015479.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michel Foucault posited that identity is sculpted by societal labels rather than an inherent human essence. He asserted that true freedom lies in critically examining and discarding these imposed identities. Today, power operates subtly through institutions dictating people's identities. Furthermore, technology and algorithms play a role in shaping digital personas, echoing Foucault's warnings. Choosing to resist these labels empowers individuals to transcend predefined identities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-michel-foucault-maybe-the-target-nowadays-is-not-to-discover-what-we-are-but-to-refuse-what-we-are-and-how-every-self-help-guru-got-it-wrong/articleshow/133015479.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/quote-of-the-day-by-michel-foucault-maybe-the-target-nowadays-is-not-to-discover-what-we-are-but-to-refuse-what-we-are-and-how-every-self-help-guru-got-it-wrong/articleshow/133015479.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T02:05:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133015542,imgsize-1216439.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote by Martha Nussbaum: 'Knowledge is no guarantee of good behavior, but ignorance is...']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133015430.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Martha Nussbaum emphasizes that possessing technical skills isn't synonymous with ethical conduct. She points out that ignorance, whether intentional or overlooked, can lead to detrimental choices. Today's educational systems may churn out proficient employees but often lack the essential elements of critical thinking and empathy. The humanities, she argues, play a crucial role in fostering understanding and reducing harm by encouraging a variety of viewpoints.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-martha-nussbaum-knowledge-is-no-guarantee-of-good-behavior-but-ignorance-is-a-virtual-guarantee-of-bad-behavior-and-how-our-education-system-forgot-the-second-half/articleshow/133015430.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-martha-nussbaum-knowledge-is-no-guarantee-of-good-behavior-but-ignorance-is-a-virtual-guarantee-of-bad-behavior-and-how-our-education-system-forgot-the-second-half/articleshow/133015430.cms]]></guid><pubDa